TDD red evidence: before the extraction hook existed, the new swap test failed to compile because extract_archive_for_test was absent. After adding only the test hook, the behavioral test was red: extraction returned Ok(()) while the expected result was Err(OllamaBundleInvalid), proving the path-based implementation could follow a parent symlink and write outside staging.

Implementation: extraction opens a stable ExtractionRoot before archive traversal. Unix anchors the root with O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC and performs every directory/file operation relative to retained directory descriptors through openat/mkdirat; child paths are never reopened through the mutable staging pathname. O_NOFOLLOW and closed error mapping reject symlink/reparse-like substitutions.

Implementation: Windows anchors the root and every created parent with FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT and handles opened without FILE_SHARE_DELETE, retaining those handles until extraction ends so the staging/parent names cannot be replaced during writes. Each opened directory/file is checked for reparse-point and directory attributes; failures are closed as invalid or storage errors. The extraction code no longer uses canonicalize plus path-based File::create.

